title: DOCKER_TLS_VERIFY is not read; tls defaults to 0 regardless
updated: 2026-08-27T15:55:35Z
---

Deliberately out of scope while karr #26 was implemented, recorded so it is a decision rather than an oversight.

The docker CLI turns TLS on from the environment: DOCKER_TLS_VERIFY=1 means 'use TLS and verify', usually paired with DOCKER_CERT_PATH. API::Docker reads DOCKER_HOST and DOCKER_CERT_PATH but not DOCKER_TLS_VERIFY, so a shell set up for the CLI reaches a tcp:// daemon in the clear unless the caller passes tls => 1 in code.

Defaulting tls from $ENV{DOCKER_TLS_VERIFY} would close that gap and match the CLI. It is a behaviour change on machines that export it (a plaintext tcp:// client would start speaking TLS), and t/tls.t asserts the default is 0 in two places, so it wants its own ticket, its own Changes line and a measurement of what a CLI-configured shell actually exports.
